  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 24pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(45.36pt, 127.7pt, "Shuttlecock velocity decay after smash and slice ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 159.38pt, "shots in badminton ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(45.36pt, 204.62pt, "Eric Collet")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.96pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(91.104pt, 200.66pt, "1,2,* ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(45.36pt, 224.06pt, "1 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(49.92pt, 227.06pt, "Univ Rennes, CNRS, IPR (Institut de Physique de Rennes) – UMR 6251; 35000 Rennes, France.  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(45.36pt, 235.22pt, "2 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(49.92pt, 238.22pt, "Institut Universitaire de France (IUF); 75231 Paris, France ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 260.54pt, "*Author to whom any correspondence should be addressed. ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 282.89pt, "E-mail: eric.collet@univ-rennes.fr ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 305.21pt, "Received xxxxxx ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 316.37pt, "Accepted for publication xxxxxx ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 327.53pt, "Published xxxxxx ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(45.36pt, 350.81pt, "Abstract ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(45.36pt, 370.25pt, "This paper reports on the decay in shuttlecock velocity after smash and slice shots performed ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 382.61pt, "by elite and international players, based on the analysis of videos captured on a badminton ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 394.97pt, "court with high-speed cameras. The trajectories of feather shuttlecocks show an exponential ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 407.45pt, "decay in velocity and an exponential increase in time-of-flight with distance, in accordance ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 419.81pt, "with the equation of motion of a shuttlecock subjected to high drag. The initial speed, which ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 433.01pt, "can exceed 500 km/h, is reduced by half every ")
  #line-at(239.21pt, 433.01pt, "3.35 m, depending on the physical ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 445.51pt, "parameters of the shuttlecock characterized by a speed index. The videos show that plastic ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 457.87pt, "shuttlecocks, which are more resistant than feather shuttlecocks, deform at high speeds. The ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 470.35pt, "resulting decay of their drag coefficient with increasing speed makes them unsuitable for ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 482.71pt, "high-level play. The study also shows that the spin induced by the slice shots of left-handed ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 495.19pt, "players or the reverse slice shots of right-handed players slows the shuttlecock down. ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 519.55pt, "Keywords: badminton, smash, velocity, drag force, time-of-flight ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(45.36pt, 580.87pt, "1. Introduction ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(56.76pt, 600.31pt, "The smash and slice in badminton are tactical shots, usually ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 612.79pt, "played from the back of the court, that often score a point. The ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 625.18pt, "smash, hit with power and speed, is also a source of fantasy ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 637.66pt, "making badminton the fastest sport in the world: P. Tan set the ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 650.02pt, "women's record at 438 km/h, while S. Rankireddy set the ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 662.38pt, "men's record at 565 km/h. Numerous studies have focused on ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 674.86pt, "the particular trajectories of shuttlecocks, which result from ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 687.94pt, "the strong aerodynamic drag experienced by these light (")
  #line-at(276.53pt, 687.94pt, "5 g) ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 701.14pt, "and elongated (")
  #line-at(114.5pt, 701.14pt, "7 cm) particles (1-8). This drag is essential ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 713.74pt, "for keeping the shuttlecock within the confines of the court, as ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 726.1pt, "it strongly decreases the velocity of the shuttlecock (9-16): an ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 738.58pt, "initial velocity of ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(114.98pt, 738.58pt, "≃")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(122.42pt, 738.58pt, "240 km/h (67 m/s) can decay within ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(265.73pt, 738.58pt, "≃")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(273.17pt, 738.58pt, "0.6 s ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 751.296pt, "to ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(55.68pt, 751.296pt, "≃")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(63.144pt, 751.296pt, "25 km/h (6.9 m/s).  ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 569.83pt, "The speed of the shuttlecock depends on the energy transfer ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 582.31pt, "between the player, the racket and the shuttlecock, as ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 594.67pt, "underlined by diverse bio-mechanical studies (17-22). ")
  #line-at(314.83pt, 607.15pt, "This article presents a quantitative analysis of the ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 619.54pt, "trajectories and velocity decay of feather and plastic ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 631.9pt, "shuttlecocks after smash shots performed by international and ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 644.38pt, "elite players. The effect of the shuttlecock's physical ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 656.74pt, "parameters, in particular its mass, is also discussed. These can ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 669.22pt, "be adapted on demand to ensure similar playing conditions ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 681.58pt, "depending on atmospheric conditions on the planet. The effect ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 693.94pt, "of slice and reverse-slice shots on velocity decay is also ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 706.42pt, "analysed, for both right- and left-handed players. Some ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 718.78pt, "tactical conclusions are discussed, based on experimental and ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 731.26pt, "theoretical results.  Considering the expected readership, the ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 743.616pt, "choice is made to use both the popular velocity unit (km/h) ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 755.976pt, "and the metric unit (m/s). ")
]

