  #line-at(314.83pt, 92.66pt, "Figure 1 shows the structure of feather shuttlecocks, ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 105.14pt, "composed of an array of diverging stems, the ends of which ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 117.5pt, "are at the convergent end of the skirt, joined together in an end ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 129.86pt, "ring. Shuttlecocks do not exhibit mirror symmetry and are ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 142.34pt, "chiral bodies (25). Due to the way the 16 feathers are placed ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 154.7pt, "into the cork, the airflow on the feathers is responsible for the ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 167.18pt, "natural counter-clockwise spinning of these projectiles as they ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 179.54pt, "propagate through the air. The centre of mass (CoM) is on the ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 192.02pt, "shuttlecock symmetry axis, close to the cork. ")
  #line-at(314.83pt, 216.74pt, "The aerodynamics of shuttlecocks was studied in several ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 229.22pt, "papers, based on wind tunnel measurements, video analysis or ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 241.58pt, "simulations (1-8, 13, 15, 26, 27). The equation of motion of a ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 254.06pt, "shuttlecock was given in many papers and here we use: ")
