  #line-at(114.5pt, 565.99pt, "curve? Figure 6 shows the velocity decay ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 578.47pt, "measured after different smash shots for two Yonex AS20 ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 590.83pt, "shuttlecocks with speed index 76/V2 and 78/V4 (table 1). The ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 603.19pt, "fit of the experimental curves with equation (6) gives similar ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 616.39pt, "initial velocities for both shots (")
  #line-at(211.73pt, 616.39pt, "320(2) km/h). The ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 628.9pt, "aerodynamic length is larger for the 78/V4 (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(238.13pt, 628.9pt, "L")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(243.65pt, 628.9pt, "=4.49(1) m) ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 641.26pt, "compared to the 76/V2 (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(152.42pt, 641.26pt, "L")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(157.94pt, 641.26pt, "=4.23(1) m). Indeed, high-speed ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 653.74pt, "shuttlecocks have lower deceleration and higher average ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 666.1pt, "speeds than low-speed ones. The shuttles have similar shapes, ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 678.58pt, "and their different aerodynamic lengths and decelarations are ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 690.94pt, "due to their mass (Table 1), which is reasonably well ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 703.42pt, "proportioned to their aerodynamic length.  ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(305.69pt, 369.41pt, "4.4 Plastic shuttlecocks ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(314.83pt, 388.85pt, "The main problem with feather shuttlecocks used in ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 401.33pt, "competition is that they are easily damaged during play. They ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 413.69pt, "therefore need to be replaced frequently to maintain their ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 426.17pt, "flight characteristics. During the last decades synthetic ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 438.53pt, "shuttlecock emerged, made from plastics, with overwhelming ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 450.91pt, "advantages in durability, cost-effectiveness, and consistency ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 463.39pt, "in recreational play (15). Plastic shuttlecocks, whose skirts are ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 475.75pt, "mainly made of nylon, are becoming increasingly popular in ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 488.23pt, "non-competitive badminton, as their flexibility gives them ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 500.59pt, "greater durability. However, this flexibility comes at the cost ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 513.07pt, "of inferior flight quality compared to feather shuttlecocks. ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 525.43pt, "Several studies have shown that the drag coefficient of ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 537.79pt, "synthetic shuttlecocks decreases with increasing speed, due to ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 550.27pt, "the large deformation of the skirt with the air pressure at high ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 562.63pt, "speed (3-5, 10, 13, 26). A recent computational study (29) ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 575.11pt, "confirmed how the cross-sectional area of the skirt decreases ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 587.47pt, "with an increase in flight speed, leading to a significant ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 599.83pt, "reduction in the drag compared to that for an undeformed ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 612.31pt, "shuttlecock. Beyond a certain speed, the deformation of the ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 624.7pt, "skirt assumes a non-axisymmetric shape with a significant ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 637.18pt, "increase in its rate of deformation with speed.  ")
  #line-at(314.83pt, 649.54pt, "The terminal velocity of the plastic shuttlecock Mavis 300 ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 661.9pt, "is lower than the one of the feathers (table 1). Therefore, a ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 674.38pt, "shorter aerodynamic length would be expected compared to ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 686.74pt, "the feather AS20 shuttles. Figure 7 shows its velocity decay ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 699.22pt, "for different initial velocities ")
