  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(303.41pt, 80.28pt, "decreases with increasing initial speed. The video 3 and  ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 92.66pt, "figure 8 show the deformation of the plastic shuttlecock from ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 105.14pt, "an initial shape with 16-fold symmetry to square or triangular ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 117.5pt, "shape after smash, due to the air pressure on the flexible skirt. ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 129.86pt, "The resulting change in the cross-section and drag coefficient ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 142.34pt, "of the shuttlecock lower the drag force. As the shuttlecock ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 154.7pt, "slows down, the air pressure on the skirt decreases and the ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 167.9pt, "initial shape is almost recovered within ")
  #line-at(478.42pt, 167.9pt, "3 meters, but the ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 180.38pt, "radius of the shuttle, and therefore the drag, still depend on ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 192.74pt, "speed (3-5, 10, 13, 26). These data, measured directly on a ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 205.22pt, "badminton court under real conditions, confirm previous ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 217.58pt, "experimental and theoretical analyses concerning the variation ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 230.06pt, "in drag coefficient as a function of initial velocity due to the ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 242.42pt, "deformation of the skirt of plastic shuttlecocks. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(305.93pt, 267.29pt, "5. Effect of slice and reverse slice on velocity decay ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(314.83pt, 279.65pt, "The slice shot is another tactical technique, known for ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 292.13pt, "causing the shuttle to spin and altering the angle of return. ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 304.49pt, "Kitta conducted experiments on feather shuttlecock (1) and ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 316.85pt, "concluded that the shuttlecock with spin experiences a ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 329.33pt, "marginally larger drag compared to shuttle without spin. A ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 341.69pt, "recent study explained why the slice shot of the left-handed  ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 354.17pt, "player (LH) is more efficient than the slice shot of the right-")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 366.53pt, "handed player (RH) (25), due to the chiral nature of a ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 378.89pt, "shuttlecock (figure 1). The helical arrangement of the feathers ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 391.37pt, "is responsible for its natural counter-clockwise rotation as it ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 403.73pt, "propagates through the air. Video 4 shows that the slice shots ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 416.21pt, "performed by right-handers induce a natural counter-")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 428.57pt, "clockwise spinning. On the contrary, the slice shots performed ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 441.07pt, "by left-handers induce an opposite clockwise spinning: the air ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 453.43pt, "flow on the feathers then stops the rotation and the ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(49.32pt, 416.33pt, "Figure 8.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(83.904pt, 416.33pt, " Deformation of the skirt of a plastic shuttlecock at high ")
  #line-at(49.32pt, 427.49pt, "speed after impact with racket, with triangular or square shapes ")
  #line-at(49.32pt, 438.65pt, "depending on initial velocity. As the shuttlecock slows down and ")
  #line-at(49.32pt, 450.55pt, "spins, the initial shape is recovered within ")
  #line-at(207.77pt, 450.55pt, "3 m.  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(49.32pt, 702.46pt, "Figure 9.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(83.904pt, 702.46pt, " Speed decay of a AS20 V3/77 shuttlecock. The ")
  #line-at(49.32pt, 713.62pt, "aerodynamic length is lower for the for a left-hander (LH) slice ")
