  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(159.38pt, 255.5pt, "4.53 m for LH reverse slice shot. ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 268.13pt, "Figure 10 shows that the situation is reversed for RH players ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 280.49pt, "(with shots performed with an AS20 76/V2 shuttlecock): the ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 293.57pt, "fit gives a longer aerodynamic length (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(203.09pt, 293.57pt, "L")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(214.13pt, 293.57pt, "4.19 m) for the RH ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 306.89pt, "slice shot than for RH reverse slice (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(193.13pt, 306.89pt, "<L>")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(217.73pt, 306.89pt, "3.21 m). Figures 9 ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 319.37pt, "and 10 show that, compared to a natural counter-clockwise ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 331.73pt, "rotation induced by a RH slice or a reverse LH slice, the ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 344.21pt, "opposite clockwise rotation induced by a LH slice or a reverse ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 356.57pt, "RH slice results in a more effective slowing down of the ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 368.93pt, "shuttlecock, which is consistent with a recent symmetry ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 381.41pt, "analysis (25). ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(45.36pt, 406.25pt, "6. Conclusion and lessons learned ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(56.76pt, 418.61pt, "This study shows that it is possible to describe with a good ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 430.97pt, "accuracy the velocity change of a badminton shuttlecock after ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 443.47pt, "smash or slice shots as an exponential decay with distance. ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 455.83pt, "The aerodynamic properties of the shuttlecocks, described ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 468.31pt, "through their speed index, allows adjusting the shuttlecock to ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 480.67pt, "the local atmospheric conditions. The speed decay is very fast ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 493.75pt, "as velocity is halved every ")
  #line-at(188.57pt, 493.75pt, "3.35 m, with important ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 506.35pt, "consequences in the game, which are of great interest for ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 518.71pt, "players or coaches.  ")
  #line-at(56.76pt, 531.07pt, "Figure 2 shows that the velocity decays is important within ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 543.55pt, "the first meter. A smash at 500 km/h from the backline is ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 556.63pt, "equivalent to a smash at ")
  #line-at(149.54pt, 556.63pt, "400 km/h shot one meter in front of ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 569.11pt, "the backline. It is therefore of tactical importance for a player ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 581.59pt, "in a defensive position, who has to lift the shuttlecock and who ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 593.95pt, "will have to face the smash of the oponent, to push the oponent ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 606.43pt, "at the back of the court.  ")
  #line-at(56.76pt, 618.82pt, "This point is evenmore interesting in terms of time-of-flight ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 631.3pt, "of the shuttlecock, which is found by intergrating equation (6): ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(45.36pt, 646.9pt, "𝑡(𝑟) =")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(77.544pt, 641.02pt, "𝐿")
  #line-at(75.864pt, 651.94pt, "𝑉")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.344pt, 653.38pt, "0")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(84.864pt, 646.9pt, "(exp (")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(110.9pt, 641.02pt, "𝑟")
  #line-at(110.9pt, 651.94pt, "𝐿")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(114.98pt, 646.9pt, ") −1)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(261.41pt, 646.9pt, "(7) ")
  #line-at(56.76pt, 663.7pt, " Figure 11 shows the measured dependence of the time-of-")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 676.06pt, "flight with distance ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(127.7pt, 676.06pt, "t(r)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(141.02pt, 676.06pt, " for a smash performed with a AS20 ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 688.54pt, "78/V4. The fit of the data with equation (7) gives ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(45.36pt, 700.9pt, "V")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(51.48pt, 701.86pt, "0")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54.72pt, 700.9pt, "=300(1) km/h for this shot, and the aerodynamic length ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(45.36pt, 713.26pt, "L")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(50.88pt, 713.26pt, "=4.48(2) m is again in good agreement with the result for ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 725.74pt, "another shot in figure 6. Figure 11 shows that the time of flight ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 489.55pt, "for an initial speed of 300 km/h increases from ")
  #line-at(509.38pt, 489.55pt, "440 ms to ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 502.87pt, "travel over 10 m to ")
  #line-at(389.95pt, 502.87pt, "660 ms to travel over 11.5 m. This also ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 515.35pt, "highlights the importance of pushing the smasher towards the ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 527.71pt, "back of the court. Indeed, for a given initial velocity ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(538.3pt, 527.71pt, "V")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(544.3pt, 528.67pt, "0")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(547.54pt, 527.71pt, ", ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 540.19pt, "increasing the distance travelled from 10 to 11.5 metres ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 552.55pt, "increases the reaction time to defend the smash by 50%.  ")
  #line-at(314.83pt, 564.91pt, "For sustainability reasons, the BWF initiative to transition ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 577.39pt, "from traditional feather shuttlecocks to synthetic-feather ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 589.75pt, "shuttlecocks has introduced equipment changes that could ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 602.23pt, "impact gameplay. The flight characteristic of plastic ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 614.59pt, "shuttlecocks with an aerodynamic length depending on the ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 626.98pt, "initial velocity, makes it difficult to control their trajectory. ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 639.46pt, "For this reason, plastic shuttlecock, which have inetresting ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 651.82pt, "longevity, cannot fully replicate the precise flight behavior of ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 664.3pt, "a high-quality natural feather shuttle. As new synthetic ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 676.66pt, "shuttlecocks made of carbon appeared recently on the market ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 689.14pt, "(30), it will be interesting to compare the flight characteristics ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 701.5pt, "and speed decay of this new generation of shuttlecocks with ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 713.86pt, "traditional feathered shuttles, which are currently the ")
  #line-at(303.41pt, 726.34pt, "benchmark for flight quality. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(309.29pt, 437.33pt, "Figure 11.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(348.43pt, 437.33pt, "  Time-of-flight of a AS20 78/V4 shuttlecock after a ")
  #line-at(309.29pt, 449.23pt, "smash shot with an initial velocity of ")
  #line-at(449.62pt, 449.23pt, "300 km/h. The time-of-")
  #line-at(309.29pt, 461.23pt, "flight increases by ")
  #line-at(382.63pt, 461.23pt, "+50% for a smash of 11.5 m ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
